#!/usr/bin/python3
"""codex-auto-resume — resume an unfinished Codex Desktop task after a usage limit resets.

Mechanism (all supported/local, no UI automation):
  * State is read through a short-lived private `codex app-server` (JSON-RPC over stdio):
    thread/read, thread/turns/list, thread/goal/get, account/rateLimits/read.
  * A usage limit is detected from the structured turn error `codexErrorInfo == usageLimitExceeded`
    (or a thread goal in status `usageLimited`).
  * Resuming = `codex queue --thread <id> --message <prompt>` (Codex's own per-thread message queue,
    drained by whichever Codex process owns the thread — normally Codex Desktop), plus, for goal
    threads, flipping the goal back to `active` so Codex's native goal loop continues by itself.
  * If the thread is not loaded anywhere, `open -g codex://threads/<id>` makes Codex Desktop load it.

Only one task can be armed at a time. Nothing is sent unless the armed thread's latest turn ended
with a usage-limit error (or the user runs `resume-now`).
"""
